ScreenCastPortal by desktop (Wayland)
  niri      on niri, install xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, then log out and back in
  gnome     install xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, GNOME's ScreenCast backend, then log out and back in
  kde       install xdg-desktop-portal-kde, KDE's ScreenCast backend, then log out and back in
  sway      install xdg-desktop-portal-wlr and a screen chooser it runs (slurp, wofi, rofi or fuzzel; without one it picks any output); choose it in ~/.config/xdg-desktop-portal/portals.conf (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.ScreenCast=wlr under [preferred]); have your compositor run `dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP`; start the portal with XDPW_PERSIST_MODE=permanent so it remembers the screen choice
  hyprland  install xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland, then log out and back in; in its screen picker, tick the box that allows a restore token so the screen choice is remembered
  river     install xdg-desktop-portal-wlr and a screen chooser it runs (slurp, wofi, rofi or fuzzel; without one it picks any output); choose it in ~/.config/xdg-desktop-portal/portals.conf (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.ScreenCast=wlr under [preferred]); have your compositor run `dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP`; start the portal with XDPW_PERSIST_MODE=permanent so it remembers the screen choice
  wayfire   install xdg-desktop-portal-wlr and a screen chooser it runs (slurp, wofi, rofi or fuzzel; without one it picks any output); choose it in ~/.config/xdg-desktop-portal/portals.conf (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.ScreenCast=wlr under [preferred]); have your compositor run `dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP`; start the portal with XDPW_PERSIST_MODE=permanent so it remembers the screen choice
  labwc     install xdg-desktop-portal-wlr and a screen chooser it runs (slurp, wofi, rofi or fuzzel; without one it picks any output); choose it in ~/.config/xdg-desktop-portal/portals.conf (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.ScreenCast=wlr under [preferred]); have your compositor run `dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP`; start the portal with XDPW_PERSIST_MODE=permanent so it remembers the screen choice
  cosmic    install xdg-desktop-portal-cosmic, COSMIC's ScreenCast backend, then log out and back in
  xfce      install xdg-desktop-portal and your desktop's ScreenCast backend (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, -kde, -wlr, -hyprland or -cosmic), then log out and back in
  mate      install xdg-desktop-portal and your desktop's ScreenCast backend (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, -kde, -wlr, -hyprland or -cosmic), then log out and back in
  cinnamon  install xdg-desktop-portal and your desktop's ScreenCast backend (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, -kde, -wlr, -hyprland or -cosmic), then log out and back in
  i3        install xdg-desktop-portal and your desktop's ScreenCast backend (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, -kde, -wlr, -hyprland or -cosmic), then log out and back in
  lxqt      install xdg-desktop-portal and your desktop's ScreenCast backend (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, -kde, -wlr, -hyprland or -cosmic), then log out and back in
  unknown   install xdg-desktop-portal and your desktop's ScreenCast backend (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, -kde, -wlr, -hyprland or -cosmic), then log out and back in
  x11 xfce  an X11 session needs no ScreenCast portal
  x11 kde   an X11 session needs no ScreenCast portal
  no display install xdg-desktop-portal and your desktop's ScreenCast backend (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, -kde, -wlr, -hyprland or -cosmic), then log out and back in
